its own app to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"application(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", made on the main actor, adds the platform’s identifier for vendor as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. It is the one identifier here that outlives a session, so add it only when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app has decided to and has the user’s consent. It is never stored or made up: on macOS and Linux,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which have none, records carry no key.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For the session an event was tracked in, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sessions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import StandardContext","import Trackers","","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.application(), .operatingSystem(), .locale(), .network()])","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","\/\/ A destination reads each value from the record's context:","\/\/ record.context[ApplicationKey.self]?.version, record.context[OperatingSystemKey.self]?.name"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers each value and the identifier for vendor in more detail."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"StandardContext"}],"title":"StandardContext","externalID":"StandardContext","symbolKind":"module"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentat